---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL } from "../lib/site";

const sections = [
  ["scope", "What these terms cover"],
  ["licence", "Licence"],
  ["warranty", "No warranty, no liability"],
  ["no-advice", "Not tax or financial advice"],
  ["responsibilities", "Your part"],
  ["third-party", "Third parties"],
  ["credits", "Credits"],
  ["trademarks", "Name and logo"],
  ["law", "Applicable law"],
  ["contact", "Contact"],
] as const;

const LICENSE_URL = `${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/main/LICENSE`;
const THIRD_PARTY_URL = `${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/blob/main/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Service · Kassiber"
  description="Kassiber is free software under AGPL-3.0. There is no service, no account, and no warranty."
  heading="Terms of Service"
  lede="Kassiber is free software you run on your own machine. There is no subscription and no service we operate for you, so these terms boil down to: the AGPL governs the code, there is no warranty, and your tax filing stays your responsibility."
  effectiveDate="2026-07-29"
  lastUpdated="2026-07-29"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="scope">
    <p class="section-number">01</p>
    <h2>What These Terms Cover</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply to this website and to the Kassiber desktop app and CLI, published by
      Bitcoin Austria (details in the{" "}<a href="/imprint">imprint</a>). There is no hosted
      Kassiber service, no accounts, and no infrastructure that holds your books. You download
      software and run it yourself, so nothing here creates a service contract, a support
      obligation, or a duty to keep publishing releases.
    </p>
    <p>
      The public nodes Kassiber offers as defaults (<a
        href="https://mempool.bitcoin-austria.at">mempool.bitcoin-austria.at</a
      >{" "}and our Fulcrum instance) are a free courtesy with no uptime guarantee. Your own node is
      the better choice anyway.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="licence">
    <p class="section-number">02</p>
    <h2>Licence</h2>
    <p>
      Kassiber is free and open source software under the
      {" "}<a href={LICENSE_URL}>GNU Affero General Public License, version 3</a>. Your rights to
      use, study, modify, and distribute it come from that licence, not from this page, and where
      the two conflict, the AGPL wins. If you redistribute a modified version over a network,
      AGPL-3.0 &sect; 13 requires you to offer users its source. Bundled components carry their own
      licences, listed in{" "}<a href={THIRD_PARTY_URL}>THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="warranty">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>No Warranty, No Liability</h2>
    <p>
      Kassiber is pre-alpha: expect crashes, breaking changes, and incorrect accounting or tax
      output. Keep independent backups and verify any number before you file it. It is given to you
      for free, by a nonprofit, with the source included so you can check our work. That is the
      whole bargain: no fee, and no assumption of your accounting risk.
    </p>
    <p class="legal-notice">
      THE SOFTWARE AND THIS WEBSITE ARE PROVIDED &ldquo;AS IS,&rdquo; WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND,
      EXPRESS OR IMPLIED (AGPL-3.0 &sect;&sect; 15&ndash;16). TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY
      LAW, BITCOIN AUSTRIA, ITS BODIES, MEMBERS, AND CONTRIBUTORS ARE NOT LIABLE FOR ANY DAMAGES
      ARISING FROM ITS USE, INCLUDING LOST OR CORRUPTED DATA, LOST BITCOIN, INCORRECT TAX OUTPUT, OR
      PENALTIES ASSESSED BY AN AUTHORITY.
    </p>
    <p>
      Liability that cannot lawfully be excluded (under Austrian law: personal injury, intent, gross
      negligence) is not excluded, and your statutory consumer rights remain unaffected.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="no-advice">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Not Tax or Financial Advice</h2>
    <p>
      Kassiber is bookkeeping software, not a tax adviser. Reports it produces, including Austrian
      &sect; 27b EStG and E 1kv output, are drafts for you and your adviser to review. You remain
      the taxpayer: the completeness of what you import, the review decisions you make, and whatever
      you file are yours. Nothing here is a recommendation to buy, sell, or hold Bitcoin.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="responsibilities">
    <p class="section-number">05</p>
    <h2>Your Part</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Keep backups of your databases and the records you imported.</li>
      <li>
        Remember your database passphrase. There is no reset and nobody holds a copy: lost
        passphrase, lost data.
      </li>
      <li>
        Verify downloads against the published SHA-256 manifest; binaries are currently unsigned.
      </li>
      <li>Review the numbers before you file, and review AI output before acting on it.</li>
      <li>Secure the machine Kassiber runs on and comply with the law that applies to you.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section id="third-party">
    <p class="section-number">06</p>
    <h2>Third Parties</h2>
    <p>
      The block explorers, Electrum servers, nodes, rate providers, and AI providers you point
      Kassiber at run under their own terms, and we are not responsible for their availability,
      accuracy, pricing, or data practices. If you configure a remote AI provider, your prompts and
      any costs are between you and them; the local-model default exists so that is a deliberate
      choice. And a reminder that should not need saying: Bitcoin transactions are irreversible.
      Kassiber is watch-only and never spends, but it cannot undo anything either.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="credits">
    <p class="section-number">07</p>
    <h2>Credits</h2>
    <p>
      Tax lot accounting is done by{" "}<a href="https://github.com/eprbell/rp2">RP2</a>, the
      open-source crypto tax engine by{" "}<a href="https://github.com/eprbell">eprbell</a>
      {" "}(Apache-2.0). Kassiber prepares, reviews, and explains; RP2 computes. We maintain a
      Bitcoin-focused{" "}<a href="https://github.com/bitcoinaustria/rp2">fork</a> with an Austrian
      &sect; 27b EStG plugin; bugs in the fork are ours, not eprbell's, and RP2's authors neither
      endorse nor warrant Kassiber. The rest of the free software we stand on is listed in
      {" "}<a href={THIRD_PARTY_URL}>THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="trademarks">
    <p class="section-number">08</p>
    <h2>Name and Logo</h2>
    <p>
      The AGPL covers the code, not the names &ldquo;Kassiber&rdquo; and &ldquo;Bitcoin
      Austria&rdquo; or the logos. Fork freely and ship your fork, but don't present your build as
      the official one. Nominative references (&ldquo;based on Kassiber&rdquo;) are fine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="law">
    <p class="section-number">09</p>
    <h2>Applicable Law</h2>
    <p>
      Austrian law applies, excluding its conflict-of-law rules and the UN Sales Convention; the
      place of jurisdiction is Vienna. If you are a consumer, mandatory protections and the courts
      of your residence are unaffected. Bitcoin Austria does not participate in consumer arbitration
      proceedings (the EU ODR platform exists at{" "}<a href="https://ec.europa.eu/odr"
        >ec.europa.eu/odr</a
      >). If a provision here is unenforceable, the rest stays in force. We update these terms when
      the project changes; your AGPL rights for versions you already received are never affected.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">10</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Bugs and feature requests go to the{" "}<a href={`${GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL}/issues`}
        >issue tracker</a
      >, vulnerabilities to a private report per the{" "}<a href="/security-policy"
        >security policy</a
      >. Everything else:
    </p>
    <address>
      <strong>Bitcoin Austria &ndash; Verein zur F&ouml;rderung von Bitcoin in &Ouml;sterreich</strong><br />
      c/o STADLER PARTNER Rechtsanw&auml;lte GmbH<br />
      Seilerst&auml;tte 24, 1010 Vienna, Austria
    </address>
    <a class="contact-link" href="mailto:office@bitcoin-austria.at">office@bitcoin-austria.at</a>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
